==Notes==
*{{LNote|race|†|The inhabitants of Skyrim during the Dragon War were variously labeled Nords{{ref|name=Paarthurnax|[[SR:Paarthurnax (dragon)|Paarthrunax]]'s dialogue in ''[[SR:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}} and Atmorans.{{ref|name=FSL2|{{Cite Book|First Servant's Letter, Page 2|ns_base=ESO}}}} The truth may lie somewhere in-between; while the two are considered distinct races,{{ref|name=TOoC|{{Cite Book|The Origin of Cyrus!|ns_base=Books}}}} the men living in the transition period between the terms' respective usage have been considered 'proto-Nords'.{{ref|name=FC|{{Cite Book|Frontier, Conquest}}}}{{ref|name=EGTS|{{Cite Book|EGT|Skyrim}}}}{{ref|name=HighKingSunstone|[[ESO:Bleakrock Isle Antiquities#High King Sunstone|High King Sunstone]] antiquity codex entry in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}}}}
* Morokei's name means '''Glorious''' in the [[Lore:Dragon Language|Dragon Language]].{{ref|name=DL|{{Cite Book|Dragon Language: Myth no More}}}}{{ref|name=SOS|{{Cite Book|Songs of Skyrim|ns_base=Skyrim}}}}

